D. Senior Management and IT Steering Committee

20. The Senior Management of the bank shall, inter alia, ensure:

(1) execution of the IT Strategy approved by the Board; (2) IT / Information Security and their support infrastructure are functioning effectively and efficiently;

(3) necessary IT risk management processes are in place and create a culture of IT risk awareness and cyber hygiene practices in the bank;

(4) cybersecurity posture of the bank is robust; and

(5) overall, IT contributes to productivity, effectiveness, and efficiency in business operations.

21. The bank shall establish an IT Steering Committee with representation at Senior Management level from IT and business functions which shall meet at least on a quarterly basis.

22. The responsibilities of IT Steering Committee, inter alia, shall be to:

(1) assist the ITSC in strategic IT planning, oversight of IT performance, and aligning IT activities with business needs;

